infographic sequence-pyramid-simple
data
  title Event-loop priority: what drains before what
  desc Both microtask tiers empty after every callback, before any macrotask phase runs
  sequences
    - label process.nextTick — highest, drained first
      desc Node-specific microtask emptied before promises; a self-rescheduling nextTick can starve the poll phase.
    - label Promise reactions — .then / await
      desc Microtask drained right after nextTick; this is why Promise.resolve().then beats setTimeout(0).
    - label Macrotasks — timers, poll (I/O), check, close
      desc The phase queues; they run only once both microtask tiers are empty, one callback at a time, no preemption.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #14b8a6
